<title>USA: Harvest winding down in Florida citrus belt - FASS.</title>
<headline>Harvest winding down in Florida citrus belt - FASS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Valencia harvest in the Florida citrus belt is winding down as supplies are running low statewide, the Florida Agricultural Statistics Service (FASS) said.</p>
<p>Most well-cared for groves continue to rate in very good condition. Caretakers are cutting cover crops that have grown tall and out of control. Summer fertilizations, sprays, and herbicides are being applied in all areas, according to FASS.</p>
<p>New crop fruit continues to make good progress and there is plenty of new foliage on most trees, FASS said.</p>
<p>-- New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1640</p>
</text>
